# Files that are executed inside Linux containers must keep LF endings no matter
# what core.autocrlf does on the machine doing the checkout. A CR at the end of
# the shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter named "/bin/sh\r", which
# fails as "not found" (exit 127) long before the script's first line runs.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
